      "Resonance Amplitude Peak: Occurs at \\omega_r = \\sqrt{\\omega_0^2 - 2\\gamma^2} (for \\gamma < \\frac{\\omega_0}{\\sqrt{2}}).",
      "Quality Factor Formula: Q = \\frac{\\omega_0}{\\Delta \\omega} = \\frac{\\omega_0}{2\\gamma}.",
      "Coupled Normal Modes: Symmetric mode (in-phase, spring unextended) and Antisymmetric mode (out-of-phase, spring active).",
      "Phase Space Area: Conserved in conservative systems by Liouville's Theorem (\\frac{d\\rho}{dt} = 0).",
      "Derivation Exam Strategy: Formulate differential equation using Newton's second law, assume trial solution x(t) = e^{\\lambda t}, and solve auxiliary quadratic characteristic equation.",
