      "Gravitational Potential of Continuous Spherical Shell: Uniform spherical shell of mass M, radius R: Outside (r \\ge R): \\Phi = -\\frac{G M}{r}, \\; g = -\\frac{G M}{r^2}; Inside (r < R): \\Phi = -\\frac{G M}{R} = \\text{constant}, \\; g = 0 (Newton's Shell Theorem).",
      "Gravitational Potential of Solid Uniform Sphere: Solid sphere of radius R: Outside (r \\ge R): \\Phi = -\\frac{G M}{r}; Inside (r \\le R): \\Phi(r) = -\\frac{G M}{2 R^3}(3 R^2 - r^2); Linear field inside g(r) = -\\frac{G M}{R^3}r.",
