  "phys-chem: bonding": {
    highlights: [
      "Band Theory of Solids (Bloch Electrons): Periodic crystalline potential splits discrete atomic valence levels into continuous energy bands; Valence Band (VB, highest occupied band) and Conduction Band (CB, lowest unoccupied band) separated by forbidden energy band gap E_g.",
      "Electrical Classification of Materials: Conductors / Metals (overlapping VB and CB or partially filled band, zero bandgap E_g = 0); Semiconductors (narrow bandgap E_g \\sim 1.1 \\text{ eV in Si}, thermal electron excitation across gap); Insulators (wide bandgap E_g > 5 \\text{ eV in diamond}).",
      "Fermi-Dirac Distribution & Fermi Level: Probability of electron state occupancy: f(E) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{(E - E_F)/k_B T}}; Fermi level E_F is chemical potential at which occupancy probability is exactly 0.5; In intrinsic semiconductors, E_F lies precisely in middle of bandgap.",
      "Drude-Lorentz Free Electron Theory of Metals: Conduction electrons treated as classical ideal electron gas; Electrical conductivity \\sigma = \\frac{n e^2 \\tau}{m_e}; Thermal conductivity K; Wiedemann-Franz Law: \\frac{K}{\\sigma T} = L = \\frac{\\pi^2}{3}\\left(\\frac{k_B}{e}\\right)^2 = 2.44 \\times 10^{-8} \\text{ W}\\Omega\\text{K}^{-2}.",
      "Intermolecular Van der Waals Forces: Dipole-dipole (Keesom orientation energy U \\propto -\\frac{\\mu^4}{r^6}); Dipole-induced dipole (Debye induction energy U \\propto -\\frac{\\mu^2 \\alpha}{r^6}); Induced dipole-induced dipole (London dispersion energy U \\propto -\\frac{\\alpha^2 I}{r^6}).",
      "Lennard-Jones (6-12) Potential: Intermolecular potential energy between neutral atoms/molecules: V(r) = 4\\epsilon \\left[ \\left(\\frac{\\sigma}{r}\\right)^{12} - \\left(\\frac{\\sigma}{r}\\right)^6 \\right]; Repulsive \\frac{1}{r^{12}} term (Pauli exclusion overlap) and attractive \\frac{1}{r^6} term (dispersion).",
      "Hydrogen Bonding Physics & Crystal Structures: Electrostatic and partially covalent interaction X-H \\cdots Y (where X, Y are highly electronegative: F, O, N); Explains anomalous expansion and density maximum of liquid water at 4°C, open cage hexagonal ice structure, and secondary structure of biological polymers.",
      "Dipole Moments & Dielectric Polarization: Molecular electric dipole moment \\vec{\\mu} = q \\vec{d}; Dielectric constant \\epsilon_r; Clausius-Mossotti relation: \\frac{\\epsilon_r - 1}{\\epsilon_r + 2} = \\frac{N \\alpha_{total}}{3\\epsilon_0}; Molar polarization P_m = \\frac{\\epsilon_r - 1}{\\epsilon_r + 2}\\frac{M}{\\rho}.",
      "Cohesive Energy of Ionic Crystals (Born-Landé Equation): Lattice energy per mole: U_0 = -\\frac{N_A M_Mad z^+ z^- e^2}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0 r_0}\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{n}\\right) where M_Mad is Madelung constant of crystal lattice geometry and n is Born exponent (5 to 12).",
      "Superconductivity & Cooper Pairing (BCS Theory): Zero electrical resistance below critical temperature T_c and expulsion of magnetic flux (Meissner effect); Mediated by electron-phonon-electron attractive pairing forming bosonic Cooper pairs with opposite spin and momentum.",
    ],
    keyPoints: [
      "Bandgap Energy Scale: Metals E_g = 0; Silicon E_g = 1.12 \\text{ eV}; Germanium E_g = 0.67 \\text{ eV}; Diamond E_g = 5.47 \\text{ eV}.",
      "Fermi-Dirac Distribution: f(E) = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{(E - E_F)/k_B T}}.",
      "Wiedemann-Franz Ratio: \\frac{K}{\\sigma T} = \\frac{\\pi^2}{3}\\left(\\frac{k_B}{e}\\right)^2 = L (Lorenz number).",
      "London Dispersion Distance Law: Attractive potential varies inversely with sixth power of distance: V_{disp} \\propto -\\frac{1}{r^6}.",
      "Lennard-Jones Equilibrium Separation: Minimum energy occurs at r_{min} = 2^{1/6}\\sigma \\approx 1.122 \\sigma.",
      "Water Density Anomaly: Maximum density at 3.98°C due to competition between thermal agitation and hydrogen-bonded cage formation.",
      "Born-Landé Lattice Energy: U_0 = -\\frac{N_A M z_1 z_2 e^2}{4\\pi \\epsilon_0 r_0}\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{n}\\right).",
      "Madelung Constant for NaCl: M_{Mad} \\approx 1.74756.",
      "Meissner Effect Condition: Magnetic field strictly expelled from superconductor interior: \\vec{B} = 0 \\implies \\chi = -1 (perfect diamagnetism).",
      "Exam Derivation Step: When deriving band classification, sketch energy levels showing filled VB, empty CB, and forbidden gap E_g.",
    ],
  },

