      "Hückel's (4n + 2) Rule for Aromaticity: Planar, fully conjugated monocyclic polyenes possessing (4n + 2) \\pi-electrons exhibit exceptional thermodynamic stabilization (aromatic: benzene n=1 with 6 \\pi, cyclopropenyl cation n=0 with 2 \\pi, cyclopentadienyl anion n=1 with 6 \\pi).",
      "Anti-Aromaticity (4n Rule): Monocyclic planar systems with 4n \\pi-electrons are destabilized relative to open-chain analogs (cyclobutadiene with 4 \\pi, cyclopentadienyl cation); Undergo Jahn-Teller rectangular geometric distortion to escape anti-aromatic degeneracy.",
      "Resonance Energy of Benzene: Heat of hydrogenation of cyclohexene \\Delta H = -120 \\text{ kJ/mol}; Hypothetical 1,3,5-cyclohexatriene expected \\Delta H = -360 \\text{ kJ/mol}; Actual benzene \\Delta H = -208 \\text{ kJ/mol}; Resonance / Delocalization stabilization energy \\approx 152 \\text{ kJ/mol} (36 kcal/mol).",
      "Conductive Conjugated Polymers: Polyacetylene (CH)_n, polyaniline, and polypyrrole; Alternating single and double bonds create half-filled \\pi band; Chemical doping (oxidation with I_2 or reduction with Na) generates charged solitons and polarons, boosting electrical conductivity to metallic regimes (>10^3 S/cm).",
      "Electrophilic Aromatic Substitution (EAS) Mechanism: Arenium ion (Wheland intermediate / \\sigma-complex) formation: Electrophile generation \\to Rate-determining attack on \\pi-system \\to Fast proton loss restoring aromaticity; Regioselectivity governed by resonance stabilization of \\sigma-complex.",
      "Directing Effects & Hammett Equation: Activating ortho/para directors (electron-donating groups -OH, -NH_2, -OCH_3, alkyl via hyperconjugation); Deactivating meta directors (electron-withdrawing groups -NO_2, -CN, -COOH, -CF_3); Halogens are deactivating but ortho/para directing due to competing -I inductive and +M resonance effects.",
      "Photochemical Reactions of Hydrocarbons (Norrish Types): Norrish Type I (homolytic alpha-cleavage of carbonyl C-C bond producing acyl and alkyl radicals); Norrish Type II (intramolecular gamma-hydrogen abstraction producing 1,4-biradical followed by fragmentation to alkene and enol).",
      "Fullerenes, Carbon Nanotubes & Graphene: Carbon allotropes: Graphene (2D honeycomb sp^2 carbon lattice, massless Dirac fermions, electron mobility >200,000 cm^2/Vs); Carbon nanotubes (rolled graphene cylinders, metallic vs semiconducting chiral vectors); C_{60} Buckminsterfullerene (truncated icosahedron).",
      "Combustion Thermodynamics of Hydrocarbon Fuels: Complete combustion: C_n H_{2n+2} + \\frac{3n+1}{2}O_2 \\to n CO_2 + (n+1) H_2O; Enthalpy of combustion \\Delta H_c; Octane rating of gasoline (isooctane = 100, n-heptane = 0) and antiknock mechanism.",
