      "Rhetorical Devices & Argumentative Fallacies: Recognizing rhetorical appeals (Ethos, Pathos, Logos); Detecting logical fallacies such as ad hominem, straw man, circular reasoning, and false dichotomies.",
      "Comparative Textual Deconstruction: Evaluating divergent viewpoints across paired articles discussing contemporary socio-economic, environmental, or scientific debates.",
      "Contextual Vocabulary Decoding: Inferring meanings of specialized terminology, archaic idioms, and figurative tropes from contextual clues and syntactic syntax.",
      "Speed Reading & Scanning Methodologies: Implementing SQ4R (Survey, Question, Read, Reflect, Recite, Review); Rapidly locating key data tables, statistical figures, and methodological qualifications.",
      "Summarization & Précis Formulation: Condensing multi-page argumentative texts into concise, coherent abstracts preserving essential logic within strict word limits (one-third length rule).",
